# Range loop with a non-integer bound

Verifies a `for` loop over `0.5..10.5` is rejected with a diagnostic stating
that range bounds must be integers through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
for (i in 0.5..10.5) {
    print(i)
}

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: for range bounds must be integers, found `decimal` at Span { start: 10, end: 13 }

<<< exit
1
